Design a combinational logic circuit comprising two outputs, f1 and f2, derived from three inputs a, b, and c. The output f1 represents the logical NOR of inputs a and b, while f2 is intended to be the XOR operation using its previous state and f1. The behavior indicates a potential misunderstanding in the sequential operation, as f2 is updated based on its own value, which may lead to unintended results if not properly controlled. Overall, the module aims to implement two distinct logical functions based on the given inputs.
