description:
Develop a current driver circuit that regulates output current based on an input voltage and a control signal. The module incorporates a capacitor filter to smooth the input voltage, which is then divided by a fixed resistance value to produce the output current. The filtered voltage is obtained by accumulating the input voltage upon the rising edge of the control signal and then right-shifting the accumulated value to scale it appropriately. This design effectively generates a controlled output current proportional to the filtered input voltage, suitable for applications requiring stable current regulation.
module top_module(
  input ctl,
  input vin,
  output iout
);

